{"tool_name":"animaltraits","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"animaltraits","home":"https://animaltraits.org","license":"CC0-1.0","summary":"AnimalTraits is a curated database containing body mass, metabolic rate and brain size measurements across a wide range of terrestrial animal taxa.","addition_date":"2022-09-02T06:43:28.607852Z","last_update_date":"2022-09-02T06:43:28.610497Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:animaltraits","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"marie.herberstein@mq.edu.au","name":"Marie E. Herberstein","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5071-2952","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Alexandra J R Carthey"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"AnimalTraits","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41597-022-01364-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022, The Author(s).Trait databases have become important resources for large-scale comparative studies in ecology and evolution. Here we introduce the AnimalTraits database, a curated database of body mass, metabolic rate and brain size, in standardised units, for terrestrial animals. The database has broad taxonomic breadth, including tetrapods, arthropods, molluscs and annelids from almost 2000 species and 1000 genera. All data recorded in the database are sourced from their original empirical publication, and the original metrics and measurements are included with each record. This allows for subsequent data transformations as required. We have included rich metadata to allow users to filter the dataset. The additional R scripts we provide will assist researchers with aggregating standardised observations into species-level trait values. Our goals are to provide this resource without restrictions, to keep the AnimalTraits database current, and to grow the number of relevant traits in the future.","authors":[{"name":"Allen A.P."},{"name":"Bulbert M."},{"name":"Buzatto B.A."},{"name":"Carthey A.J.R."},{"name":"Eldridge M.D.B."},{"name":"Falster D."},{"name":"Fernandez Winzer L."},{"name":"Griffith S.C."},{"name":"Herberstein M.E."},{"name":"Khan M.K."},{"name":"Lowe E."},{"name":"Madin J.S."},{"name":"McLean D.J."},{"name":"Narendra A."},{"name":"Smith K."},{"name":"Westoby M."},{"name":"Whiting M.J."},{"name":"Wolff J.O."},{"name":"Wright I.J."}],"date":"2022-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Scientific Data","title":"AnimalTraits - a curated animal trait database for body mass, metabolic rate and brain size"},"pmcid":"PMC9163144","pmid":"35654905"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data submission, annotation and curation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0219"},{"term":"Ecology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0610"},{"term":"Endocrinology and metabolism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3407"},{"term":"Evolutionary biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3299"},{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"AnimalTraits","home":"https://bio.tools/animaltraits","license":"CC0-1.0","summary":"AnimalTraits is a curated database containing body mass, metabolic rate and brain size measurements across a wide range of terrestrial animal taxa.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:animaltraits/db/animaltraits.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"